the protest organized by the family was  much larger than expected  thousands throughout brazil calling for  justice for moise cabangambe a congolese  migrant whose face is now everywhere  he's become a symbol for the black lives  matter movement  moisea was brutally beaten to death in  this beach kiosk where he used to work  it's in the same neighborhood where  president jair bolsonaro owns a house  this neighborhood is where brazil's  elite lives he was treated like an  animal like a thing just because he was  claiming two days of overdue wages some  twenty dollars  we're all here because we want black  people to be treated like humans moyes  could have been my son my brother my  cousin  cctv released by the police show moise  arguing with a man he was taken down by  others beaten with a club and a baseball  bat and tied to a pole  black people represent more than half of  brazil's population the largest number  outside of africa  [Music]  what has changed since the times of  slavery moyes was tied and beaten to  death in public as if he were a thing  moyes's family fled the warren congo in  2014  his mother asked for justice and peace  we ran away from violence in a civil war  to find more violence  suzette gomez a teacher and activist  says moyes's tragic death is now uniting  brazilians against discrimination  we have to unite and fight for  minorities indigenous people black  people gay people  the murder happened during an electoral  year with president bolsonaro aiming for  a second term  but these protesters say that the  president's silence shows how little he  has done to protect minorities  manuka yanakiv al-jazeera
 

